    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Flynn Estate Agents are delighted to bring number 37B Hayestown, Rush to the open market for sale. Newly built in 2024, this impressive A3-rated, 3 bed, 3 bath home with an attic conversion has been lovingly maintained and thoughtfully designed to cater for modern living. Set on a generously sized south-facing plot within the highly sought-after Hayestown development, the property effortlessly combines contemporary style with an exceptional location, offering a comfortable, energy-efficient lifestyle ideal for growing families and discerning buyers alike. Total floor area is approximately 103.80 sqm, plus 39 sqm of attic space (142.8 sqm overall).\n\nUpon entering, you are greeted by a bright and spacious hall that immediately sets the tone for the quality and finish throughout. Three well-proportioned bedrooms are conveniently accessed from the hallway. The main bedroom is a generous double, complete with the added convenience of an en-suite bathroom. Bedroom two is another spacious double, while bedroom three is perfectly suited for use as a single bedroom. \n\nTo the rear, the open-plan kitchen and dining area form the true heart of the home, providing an inviting space for everyday living as well as entertaining. Flooded with natural light, this area features sliding doors that open seamlessly onto the rear garden, creating an ideal indoor-outdoor connection. Adjacent to this, the cosy living room offers a peaceful and comfortable retreat, perfect for relaxing and unwinding. A well-appointed family bathroom and separate utility room complete the ground floor. The thoughtfully converted attic further enhances the home`s appeal, offering three versatile rooms and a stylish bathroom. This adaptable space is ideal for a variety of uses including a gym or home office. \n\nHayestown is ideally situated close to the heart of Rush, with a range of shops, pubs and restaurants, as well as the Millbank Theatre and local library. The area offers an abundance of sports and recreational facilities nearby, including yacht and sailing clubs, cricket, golf, and GAA clubs. Residents can enjoy both South and North Beach within minutes. The village is also convenient to Skerries and Lusk, and offers easy commuting access to Dublin Airport and the City Centre. The area is well served by bus and rail links and is a short drive from the M1 and M50 motorways.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway\n-With laminate wood floor\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.82m (12'6\") x 3.44m (11'3\")\n-With laminate wood floor \n-En-Suite\n\nEn-Suite - 1.68m (5'6\") x 2.54m (8'4\")\n-Tiled floor & partially tiled walls\n-WC and WHB\n-Shower cubicle\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.91m (12'10\") x 3.49m (11'5\")\n-With laminate floor\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.06m (6'9\") x 3.44m (11'3\")\n-With laminate floor\n\nBathroom - 2.78m (9'1\") x 2.22m (7'3\")\n-Tiled floor & partially tiled walls\n-WC and WHB\n-Shower cubicle\n-Panel bath with overhead shower attachments\n\n\nLounge - 3.73m (12'3\") x 3.87m (12'8\")\n-With laminate wood floor\n-Feature fireplace with stove insert\n\nKitchen/Diner - 4.97m (16'4\") x 5.91m (19'5\")\n-With laminate wood floor\n-With a range of matching floor and eye level fitted press units\n-Tiled splashbacks\n-Integrated appliances\n-Space and plumbing for washing machine and dishwasher\n-Sliding door to rear garden\n\nUtility Room - 2.57m (8'5\") x 1.05m (3'5\")\n-With laminate wood floor \n-Plumbed for appliences\n\nAttic Room 1 - 5.34m (17'6\") x 5.87m (19'3\")\n-With carpet\n\nAttic Room 2 - 3.76m (12'4\") x 2.87m (9'5\")\n-With carpet\n\nAttic Room 3 - 5.06m (16'7\") x 3.34m (10'11\")\n-With carpet\n\nBathroom - 2.29m (7'6\") x 2.78m (9'1\")\n-Fully tiled \n-WC & WHB\n\n"
      },
